{
  "original_id": "primary-20260914-q-product-unimodality",
  "archive_id": "BW2-PR20260914-q_product_unimodality",
  "title": "A two-factor criterion for unimodality of stretched q-integer products",
  "batch_label": "primary-20260914",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For every integer r>=2 and all positive integers a,c,b, define [a]_q=sum_{i=0}^{a-1}q^i and [b]_(q^r)=sum_{j=0}^{b-1}q^(rj). The full integer-indexed coefficient sequence of [a]_q[c]_q[b]_(q^r), including zero coefficients, is weakly unimodal if and only if r divides a, or r divides c, or b<=1+floor(a/r)+floor(c/r). The disjunction is inclusive and factor-1 cases are included. This is exactly the k=2 restriction of the original Conjecture 5.4; no assertion resolving its other parameter ranges is submitted.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
